content='```yaml\n---\n- name: Restore etcd - get all nodes\n  command: kubectl get nodes --no-headers -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name\n  register: all_nodes_output\n\n- name: Restore etcd - remove old nodes\n  command: kubectl delete node "{{ item }}"\n  loop: "{{ old_nodes | difference(all_nodes_output.stdout_lines) }}"\n```\n\nThis playbook starts by retrieving the list of all current nodes in the cluster using `kubectl get nodes`. It excludes headers and registers the output. The second task uses this list to identify and delete any old nodes that are no longer part of the cluster, by comparing the list of old nodes to the current nodes.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'phi4:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-23T04:15:38.81498229Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 4185751338, 'load_duration': 2124586755, 'prompt_eval_count': 330, 'prompt_eval_duration': 256798006, 'eval_count': 144, 'eval_duration': 1803447770, 'model_name': 'phi4:14b'} id='run--4e33fb2a-a077-442e-9307-f304e2193874-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 330, 'output_tokens': 144, 'total_tokens': 474}
